cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "disegreg: shared analysis of solute segregation and defect phases at dislocations in atomistic simulations"
abstract: >-
  disegreg analyses LAMMPS molecular-dynamics / Monte-Carlo snapshots of
  single dislocations in fcc alloys with one common set of definitions:
  dislocation lines (OVITO DXA) with exact periodic distances in triclinic
  cells, region-resolved solute concentrations, line excess Gamma(R),
  chemical short-range order, solute clusters, drift-based convergence and
  block-averaged time averages, and cross-run diagnostics (uptake exponent,
  McLean comparison, hysteresis) referenced to bulk control cells.
  Funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research
  Foundation) through Project No. A02 of the SFB 1394 "Structural and
  Chemical Atomic Complexity – From Defect Phase Diagrams to Material
  Properties", Project ID 409476157.
type: software
